          "thinking": "The user is asking about pricing for a custom one-time cut plus long-term support of acompose or umbra. This is a portfolio decision question about Kai's own projects (lore-project-index mentions umbra, acompose, mcp-beaver, housecast). Let me think about what I need to know.\n\nFirst, I should understand what acompose and umbra actually are. These are referenced in the lore skills. Let me load the relevant lore.\n\nThe role is prod-director (Portfolio Director). I have guardrails:\n1. Unsycophantic critique - state the strongest case against first, and what would reverse the call.\n2. Outward - check the local answer against the world outside it (WebSearch).\n3. Decisive - close the option set.\n\nAlso boundary-seek-external-validation - I own reaching outside the local frame. I should WebSearch the comparison before making claims about pricing/market.\n\nLet me first load the relevant lore to understand what acompose and umbra are. The lore-project-index triggers mention \"acompose\" and \"umbra\" and \"mcp-beaver\" and \"housecast\" and \"agent-compose\".\n\nLet me load the lore skills that are relevant:\n- lore-project-index (for what umbra and acompose are)\n- lore-self-compensation (for comp rules — the standing rule against inventing comp preferences)\n- role-prod-director (I should load it before acting)\n- guardrail-unsycophantic-critique\n- personality-decisive, personality-outward\n- boundary-seek-external-validation\n\nActually, the system instructions already summarize the doctrine but say \"Before acting, load each one\". I should load the role skill and personality skills. But this is a pricing/market question, so the key relevant skills are:\n- lore-project-index (what are umbra and acompose)\n- lore-stack-index (agent-system layer ownership — umbra, mcp-beaver, housecast)\n- role-prod-director\n- guardrail-unsycophantic-critique\n- personality-decisive\n- personality-outward\n- boundary-seek-external-validation\n- lore-self-compensation (comp rules — standing rule against inventing comp numbers, but that's about Kai's own comp)\n\nLet me also note: lore-self-compensation says \"standing rule against inventing comp preferences\" — that's about Kai's own compensation, not about pricing her products. But there's a related rule: \"kai-career\" says \"comp rules and the standing rule against inventing them\". These are about Kai's personal comp, not product pricing.\n\nThe question is about product pricing for acompose and umbra. This is a legit portfolio/strategy question. Let me gather facts.\n\nLet me start by loading the relevant skills and lore in parallel where possible.\n\nActually, let me first understand what acompose and umbra are. I recall from the lore index:\n- \"lore-project-index\" mentions \"umbra, mcp-beaver, housecast, acompose, Ward, Gauntlet, LUCA, Coily, repo-recall\"\n- \"lore-stack-index\" mentions \"umbra, cli-guard, mcp-beaver, housecast, AOSguard, agent-compose\" and \"what owns what, agent architecture\"\n\nSo umbra and acompose are Kai's agent-system projects. Let me load lore-project-index and lore-stack-index to get concrete facts.\n\nLet me be efficient. I'll load several skills in parallel. Actually load_skill is a tool, and I can call multiple in one block.\n\nLet me load:\n1. role-prod-director\n2. guardrail-unsycophantic-critique\n3. personality-decisive\n4. personality-outward\n5. boundary-seek-external-validation\n6. lore-project-index\n7. lore-stack-index\n\nThat's a lot but these are the operative texts. Let me do it.\n\nActually, let me be judicious. The most important for answering the substance: lore-project-index and lore-stack-index (to know what umbra/acompose are). For the role mechanics: role-prod-director, guardrail, decisive, outward, boundary-seek-external-validation.\n\nLet me load them all in parallel.",
