                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1.\ntitle       Multi-Agent Orchestration 2026: A Benchmark of Latency and ...\nhref        https://www.refactor.website/artificial-intelligence/multi-agent-orchestration-2026-latency-cost-benchmarks\nbody        Jan 30, 2026 · An exhaustive benchmark of 2026 multi-agent orchestration\n            frameworks, comparing latency, throughput, and operational costs\n            for frontier models like GPT-5 and Gemini 3.\n2.\ntitle       Pricing | AI Agent Orchestration\nhref        https://ai-agent-orchestration.com/pricing.html\nbody        Pricing depends on scope: how many agent types the pipeline needs, how many\n            systems it has to talk to, and whether you're deploying onto\n            Kubernetes infrastructure you already run or need that built\n            alongside it.\n3.\ntitle       AI Agent Orchestration: Proven Frameworks, Trade-Offs, and ...\nhref        https://nexaitech.com/ai-agent-orchestration/\nbody        Sep 2, 2025 · Scaling SaaS and FinTech teams need ai agent orchestration\n            beyond demos. Compare LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, and other\n            enterprise platforms like AWS Bedrock with trade-offs for\n            production AI.\n4.\ntitle       Multi-Agent Orchestration Frameworks: Complete Comparison ...\nhref        https://www.accio.com/wow/guide-multi-agent-orchestration-frameworks.html\nbody        Instead of building every agent persona from scratch, developers are\n            increasingly \"importing\" specialized agents—like a \"SEC Compliance\n            Agent\" or a \"React Performance Auditor\"—and then using an\n            orchestration framework to glue them together.\n5.\ntitle       Best Multi-Agent Orchestration Frameworks for Enterprise AI ...\nhref        https://wizr.ai/blog/best-multi-agent-orchestration-frameworks/\nbody        Jul 20, 2026 · Compare best Multi-Agent Orchestration Frameworks for\n            Enterprise AI in 2026. Evaluate features, scalability, governance,\n            & deployment to choose right framework.\n6.\ntitle       Best Multi-agent Orchestration Frameworks in 2026\nhref        https://www.truefoundry.com/blog/multi-agent-orchestration-frameworks\nbody        Jun 16, 2026 · Compare the top multi-agent orchestration frameworks by\n            orchestration model, production readiness, and what each one\n            leaves unresolved at enterprise scale.\n=====\n1.\ntitle       AI Agent Sandboxes: 26 Providers Compared | engine.build\nhref        https://engine.build/lab/agent-sandboxes\nbody        June 28, 2026 - Free tier available; paid plans start at $50/month plus usage\n            ($0.04/vCPU-hour, $0.013/GiB-memory-hour). ... Not a generic\n            sandbox, a deployment platform for long-running, stateful agents,\n            closer to Vercel than E2B.\n2.\ntitle       LLM Pricing: Top 15+ Providers Compared\nhref        https://aimultiple.com/llm-pricing\nbody        Bundled apps: agent building with ... over deployed agents. The free plan\n            offers limited access to Grok. SuperGrok Lite ($10/month) is the\n            entry paid tier.... Published: 1 month ago\n3.\ntitle       What is an AI sandbox? | Blog — Northflank\nhref        https://northflank.com/blog/what-is-an-ai-sandbox\nbody        January 17, 2026 - Configure isolation, Northflank automatically provisions\n            microVM-backed infrastructure with secure defaults · For teams\n            with specific requirements, book a demo with Northflank's\n            engineering team to discuss custom configurations, enterprise\n            features, or high-volume pricing. ... AI sandboxes are no longer\n            optional (or, in our opinion, ever were). They're now fundamental\n            to building safe, scalable AI applications. As AI agents become\n            more autonomous and code execution becomes more prevalent, proper\n            isolation is a must for any production-ready products.\n4.\ntitle       Best Cloud Sandboxes for AI Agents in 2026 | Blaxel Blog\nhref        https://blaxel.ai/blog/best-cloud-sandboxes-ai-agents-2026\nbody        April 20, 2026 - Co-located agent hosting eliminates network round-trip\n            latency between the agent and its sandbox. Both run on the same\n            infrastructure. The platform holds ISO 27001 certification, SOC 2\n            Type II certification with HIPAA support available through a BAA.\n            Sandboxes transition to standby after inactivity. Blaxel's feature\n            set addresses three production requirements: persistent state,\n            fast resume, and secure isolation. Perpetual standby: Sandboxes\n            remain in standby indefinitely with no compute charges during\n            standby.\n5.\ntitle       Top 7 AI agent runtime tools and platforms in 2026 | Blog — Northflank\nhref        https://northflank.com/blog/top-ai-agent-runtime-tools\nbody        March 4, 2026 - Supports microVM-based isolation (Kata Containers,\n            Firecracker, and gVisor), on-demand GPUs, self-service BYOC across\n            AWS, GCP, Azure, Oracle, CoreWeave, on-premises, and bare-metal,\n            and both ephemeral and persistent environments with no forced time\n            limits. In production since 2021 across startups, public\n            companies, and government deployments. E2B - Purpose-built sandbox\n            tool for AI agents and LLM apps. Firecracker microVMs, Python and\n            TypeScript SDKs, sessions up to 24 hours on paid tiers.\n6.\ntitle       10 Best Code Execution Sandboxes for AI Agents (2026) | Fastio\nhref        https://fast.io/resources/best-code-execution-sandboxes-ai-agents/\nbody        July 15, 2026 - We compared them to help you estimate production costs.\n            Maximum security: Northflank or E2B. Both use Firecracker microVMs\n            for kernel-level isolation. GPU workloads: Modal or Beam Cloud.\n            Both offer A100/H100 access for ML inference and training. Fastest\n            cold starts: Cloudflare Sandboxes (sub-50ms) or Blaxel (25ms\n            resume from standby).",
                  "annotations": {
                    "priority": 0.0
                  }
                }
              ],
              "structuredContent": {
                "stdout": "1.\ntitle       Multi-Agent Orchestration 2026: A Benchmark of Latency and ...\nhref        https://www.refactor.website/artificial-intelligence/multi-agent-orchestration-2026-latency-cost-benchmarks\nbody        Jan 30, 2026 · An exhaustive benchmark of 2026 multi-agent orchestration\n            frameworks, comparing latency, throughput, and operational costs\n            for frontier models like GPT-5 and Gemini 3.\n2.\ntitle       Pricing | AI Agent Orchestration\nhref        https://ai-agent-orchestration.com/pricing.html\nbody        Pricing depends on scope: how many agent types the pipeline needs, how many\n            systems it has to talk to, and whether you're deploying onto\n            Kubernetes infrastructure you already run or need that built\n            alongside it.\n3.\ntitle       AI Agent Orchestration: Proven Frameworks, Trade-Offs, and ...\nhref        https://nexaitech.com/ai-agent-orchestration/\nbody        Sep 2, 2025 · Scaling SaaS and FinTech teams need ai agent orchestration\n            beyond demos. Compare LangChain, CrewAI, AutoGen, and other\n            enterprise platforms like AWS Bedrock with trade-offs for\n            production AI.\n4.\ntitle       Multi-Agent Orchestration Frameworks: Complete Comparison ...\nhref        https://www.accio.com/wow/guide-multi-agent-orchestration-frameworks.html\nbody        Instead of building every agent persona from scratch, developers are\n            increasingly \"importing\" specialized agents—like a \"SEC Compliance\n            Agent\" or a \"React Performance Auditor\"—and then using an\n            orchestration framework to glue them together.\n5.\ntitle       Best Multi-Agent Orchestration Frameworks for Enterprise AI ...\nhref        https://wizr.ai/blog/best-multi-agent-orchestration-frameworks/\nbody        Jul 20, 2026 · Compare best Multi-Agent Orchestration Frameworks for\n            Enterprise AI in 2026. Evaluate features, scalability, governance,\n            & deployment to choose right framework.\n6.\ntitle       Best Multi-agent Orchestration Frameworks in 2026\nhref        https://www.truefoundry.com/blog/multi-agent-orchestration-frameworks\nbody        Jun 16, 2026 · Compare the top multi-agent orchestration frameworks by\n            orchestration model, production readiness, and what each one\n            leaves unresolved at enterprise scale.\n=====\n1.\ntitle       AI Agent Sandboxes: 26 Providers Compared | engine.build\nhref        https://engine.build/lab/agent-sandboxes\nbody        June 28, 2026 - Free tier available; paid plans start at $50/month plus usage\n            ($0.04/vCPU-hour, $0.013/GiB-memory-hour). ... Not a generic\n            sandbox, a deployment platform for long-running, stateful agents,\n            closer to Vercel than E2B.\n2.\ntitle       LLM Pricing: Top 15+ Providers Compared\nhref        https://aimultiple.com/llm-pricing\nbody        Bundled apps: agent building with ... over deployed agents. The free plan\n            offers limited access to Grok. SuperGrok Lite ($10/month) is the\n            entry paid tier.... Published: 1 month ago\n3.\ntitle       What is an AI sandbox? | Blog — Northflank\nhref        https://northflank.com/blog/what-is-an-ai-sandbox\nbody        January 17, 2026 - Configure isolation, Northflank automatically provisions\n            microVM-backed infrastructure with secure defaults · For teams\n            with specific requirements, book a demo with Northflank's\n            engineering team to discuss custom configurations, enterprise\n            features, or high-volume pricing. ... AI sandboxes are no longer\n            optional (or, in our opinion, ever were). They're now fundamental\n            to building safe, scalable AI applications. As AI agents become\n            more autonomous and code execution becomes more prevalent, proper\n            isolation is a must for any production-ready products.\n4.\ntitle       Best